  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\nThis strategy optimizes step function coefficients by focusing on three key modifications: adaptive scaling, content-aware adjustments, and multi-stage refinement. Unlike previous Gaussian/bell-shaped approaches, we use a two-phase process: (1) short-term Adam optimization with larger smoothing for robustness, and (2) long-term Frank-Wolfe method with direct gradient checks against the real objective via FFT convolution. The algorithm prioritizes peak reduction in the convolution spectrum while maintaining normalization. This approach is motivated by the observation that previous solutions over-relied on specific shapes without leveraging real gradient feedback.\n\n2. Mathematical specification\nFor a sequence a of length n:\n- Objective: min(2 * n * max(convolve(a, a, mode='full')) / (sum(a))^2)\n- Constraints: a[i] >= 0, sum(a) >= 0.01\nThe Frank-Wolfe method is used for its sparsity-inducing property, with gradients computed via \u03a9(a) = convolve(a, g) where g solves the dual program. Adam optimization handles initial setup with a smoothed projection, and \u0394t adaptive time pacing ensures high-frequency checks without overspending.\n\n3. Implementation procedure\n- Initialize sequence of length 640 (balanced and efficient)\n- Phase1: Adam-bound 50s per iteration with \u03c4_max scaling (default \u03c4_max = 0.8)\n- Phase2: Frank-Wolfe with \u03c4_max = 1.2 (higher smoothing for initial escape)\n- Automated time management system: total time 1800s divided into batches, with early termination if sum halts\n- Intermediate reshaping (shifted if not improving)\n\n4. Search choices and variations\n- Key hyperparameters: smoothing factors, time per step, threshold values\n- Smooth variations include: \n  \u2022 Adaptive \u03c4 max (initial \u03c4_max = 0.85 * max(conv))\n  \u2022 Temperature \u03c4 starting at 1.0 (when cooling is needed)\n- Jump in improvements: \n  \u2022 Increase smoothing factor when conv peaks detected\n  \u2022 Shift indices if not improving\n\n5. Compute budget and robustness\n- Initial: Adam 300s, Frank-Wolfe 500s, total 800s for setup\n- Adam iterations: min per update 50s (batched)\n- Frank-Wolfe iterations: min 500s per candidate\n- FFT call at every non-bound step:\n  \u2022 Cost O(n log n) is handled internally\n\n6. Validation and return contract\n- Evaluator step:\n  \u2022 Check sequence normalized and sum >=0.01 via assert\n  \u2022 Compute exact max convolution with numpy FFT\n- Print statements:\n  \u2022 Display every candidate's 2*n*max/sum\u00b2 score\n  \u2022 Indicate time used per iteration\n- Return only improved candidate sequences with explicit higher bounds",
